  - special-fibre
  - projective-gluing
abstract: >-
  Working v33 checks the three-open polynomial-spectrum gluing of
  Proj(ReesMod2), with abstract pullback overlaps and no polynomial
  product-overlap presentation. CompatChart2t (191 lines) proves the
  quotient-induced divided chart; CompatChartXt and CompatChartYt
  (105 lines each) prove graph-ideal saturations. CompatPolynomialRestrictions
  proves six directed polynomial-to-abstract restrictions;
  SpecialFibrePolynomialCover makes the three spectra literal cover
  objects; SpecialFibreGluing (167 lines) checks six Spec.map squares,
  a triple cocycle, and Proj(ReesMod2) ≅ Glue(S_2t/(2), S_Xt/(2),
  S_Yt/(2)). TateEvenBranchGenericFibre (59 lines) packages the actual
  blow-up generic-fibre isomorphism over D(2). The existing 2,249-line
  TateEvenBranch chart file was not refactored. All seven targeted files
  passed direct lake env lean checks with only propext, Classical.choice,
  and Quot.sound in their axiom reports; the scoped sorry scan is empty.
  A full lake build BealGeneral is unverified; the large standalone
  special-fibre source check timed out without diagnostic. Neither
  a global identification of the actual special-fibre pullback with
  the quotient Proj nor a degree-one/nonzero-overline(2t) certificate
  is advertised. This is not a general Beal proof. The scoped v33
  README check covered three Beal directories; the prior 80-directory
  project-wide audit used a different scope.
